  "worked_solution": "Since $(b,8)$ is the point of intersection of the two lines, the values $x=b,\\,y=8$ must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=-2x+2 \\\\ y=-5x-a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=b,\\,y=8$ to obtain a new system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}8=-2(b)+2 \\\\ 8=-5(b)-a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system simplifies as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}8=-2b+2 \\\\ 8=-5b-a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we know that $b=-3.$ Then, we can substitute $b=-3$ into the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =-5b-a \\\\ 8 & =-5(-3)-a \\\\ 8 & =15-a \\\\ -7 & =-a \\\\ 7 & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=7$ and $b=-3.$",
